in"],"min":[["OS","Windows XP, Windows Vista, Windows 7 or Windows 8"],["Processor","2 GHz dual core"],["Memory","2 GB RAM"],["Graphics","NVIDIA GeForce 8000 series or ATI Radeon HD 2000 series or better"],["DirectX","Version 9.0c"],["Storage","17 GB available space"],["Sound Card","100% DirectX 9.0c compatible sound device"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows 7 or Windows 8"],["Processor","AMD Phenom II X4 or Intel Core 2 Quad or better"],["Memory","2 GB RAM"],["Graphics","AMD Radeon HD 5850"],["DirectX","Version 9.0c"],["Storage","17 GB available space"],["Sound Card","100% DirectX 9.0c compatible sound device"]],"deck":2,"blurb":"Adam Jensen, a former SWAT specialist, works security for a biotechnology company until armed attackers raid the facility and kill the scientists he was hired to protect. Deus Ex: Human Revolution casts the player as Jensen, rebuilt with mechanical augmentations and drawn into a conspiracy across a near-future world split between people who can afford such upgrades and those who cannot.\n\nLevels leave room for different approaches, including stealth, direct combat, hacking and conversation, and the game mixes action with role-playing progression. This Director's Cut is a revised edition of the original. It is single-player with full controller support, and it suits fans of immersive sims who like to choose how a problem gets solved."}}